      "message": "fix(post): canned-cycle posts traverse between holes at the stream's hop\n\nThe six cycle-writing posts (fanuc, haas, mazak, tormach, doosan-dnm,\nsinumerik) swallowed every rapid after a cycle until the section ended,\nand read G98 with the tool already on R. So the traverse between holes\nand the exit from the last one ran at the R plane, below the hop the\npath was verified at.\n\nA cycle's chain is now only what stays on its hole (its XY, at or below\nR). The first rapid leaving it ends the group with G80 and posts as the\nstream says. Each hole returns to R: G99 when a group opens, and\nSinumerik is seated on R so either return mode lands there. A cycle read\noff its hole is seated from the stream's position (up to R first when\nbelow it), and a cut leaving the hole inside a group is refused by name.\n\nPinned by crates/post/tests/cycle_hop.rs, a read-back checker run on all\nsix posts, and by #1002's drill_retract goldens (out of KNOWN_BUGS). The\napp NC goldens of the drilling programs are regenerated and read.\n\nFixes #994\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
