      "message": "fix(post): seat a cycle read away from its hole at the section's hop\n\nTwo latent seat gaps in the six canned-cycle mill posts (fanuc, haas,\nmazak, sinumerik, tormach, doosan-dnm), from the review of #1019:\n\n- A cycle record read away from its hole with no stream rapid to it\n  (back-to-back cycle records) was seated by an XY move at the current\n  Z - R after a G99 hole. The away seat now climbs to the section's\n  PARAM RetractPlane (max with R), moves over the hole, then descends\n  to R; a section that states no RetractPlane is refused by name.\n- Probe moves (onProbeMove/onProbeRetreat/onProbeGuard) did not set\n  seatKnown, so a cycle after probing as a section's first motion was\n  not seated. They now call probeSeat(), which also closes an open\n  cycle group with G80.\n\nPinned in crates/post/tests/cycle_hop.rs on all six posts.\n\nHELD: conformance's synth_* stream is exactly a back-to-back stream\nwith no RetractPlane, so it is now refused; see #1028.\n\nRefs #1028\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
